===Pronunciation===
{{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈpɒ.lɪ.siː.mi/|lang=en}}, {{IPAchar|/pə.ˈlɪ.sɪ.mi/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|polysemies}}

# {{lb|en|semantics}} The ability of [[word]]s, [[sign]]s and [[symbol]]s to have [[multiple]] [[meaning]]s.
#* {{quote-book|title=Polysemy: Flexible Patterns of Meaning in Mind and Language|page=3|author=Brigitte Nerlich|year=2011|passage=Fifty years ago the linguist and semanticist Stephen Ullmann wrote that '''polysemy''', the fact that some words have a network of multiple but related meanings, is "the pivot of semantic analysis" (Ullmann 1957 [1951]: 117).}}

